## 🐳 Docker

Because this project injects environment variables at runtime, you only need to build the Docker image once. You can deploy the exact same image to staging and production just by changing the container's environment variables.

Build the Docker image:

```bash
docker build -t {{ project_name | lower | replace('_', '-') | replace(' ', '-') }} .
```

Run the container locally:

```bash
{% if use_oidc %}
docker run -it --rm -p 8080:8080 --env-file .env \
	-e OIDC_AUTHORITY="{% if oidc_provider == 'Local Keycloak' %}http://localhost:9080/realms/my-app{% else %}{{ oidc_authority }}{% endif %}" \
	-e OIDC_CLIENT_ID="{% if oidc_provider == 'Local Keycloak' %}my-react-spa{% else %}{{ oidc_client_id }}{% endif %}" \
	{{ project_name | lower | replace('_', '-') | replace(' ', '-') }}
{% else %}
docker run -it --rm -p 8080:8080 --env-file .env {{ project_name | lower | replace('_', '-') | replace(' ', '-') }}
{% endif %}
```

